module Core

### Represents the protocol for unchecked subtraction.
### `UncheckedSubtractable` is for types whose subtraction surface deliberately
### skips the overflow / underflow check. The operation maps to LLVM
### `sub nsw`/`nuw`, which lets the optimizer assume underflow never occurs;
### violations are undefined behavior.
protocol UncheckedSubtractable
  ### Returns the unchecked difference of this value and `you`.
  ### Underflow / overflow are undefined behavior; the caller must prove the
  ### operation stays in range.
  ### :param you: The value to subtract.
  ### :returns: The resulting `Me` value.
  @readonly
  dangerous routine Me.sub_unchecked(you: Me) -> Me
